      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: give repair workers coherent timeout budgets",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- define one safely parsed and bounded timeout contract for repair Codex workers\n- default each repair Codex worker to 30 minutes and the internal/workflow execute-fix step to 70 minutes\n- raise the execute job to 75 minutes, retaining five minutes for cleanup and reporting\n- reserve meaningful capacity for validation, review, and fix workers after a long edit pass\n- include focused numeric-bound, budget-invariant, long-edit, workflow-default, and deterministic CI-fixture coverage\n\n## Recovery Context\n\nThis reproduces the exact eight-file tree previously completed in isolated repair commits `c54845a` and `67514e1`. That tree passed the full configured changed-surface gate; the prior run lost only the final publication step when its enclosing review timeout was exhausted.\n\nImplementation requested and reproduced by @Takhoffman in https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/issues/487.\n\n## Safety\n\nThe change preserves bounded attempts, pinned-base editing, deterministic final base synchronization, exact-head checks, CI and merge gates, credential boundaries, durable status updates, cleanup, and failure reporting. It does not change authentication, approvals, sandboxing, or trust-boundary semantics, and it does not edit `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pnpm check:changed` on Node 24 or newer\n- final Codex `/review` on the exact validated head before publication\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/clawsweeper/issues/487\n",
